\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A signed sum with integral coefficients}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For an alternating form on #{4} coordinates, the familiar
matching expression is
#{A_{12}A_{34}-A_{13}A_{24}+A_{14}A_{23}}, as in
\ref{fdip-00MD}. Each term uses every index once.
The [finite exterior polynomial](fdip-00TF) makes the same
kind of selection without factorial division. How does its
top coefficient extend the matching convention over a ring?}
